NAME
       hexdump - display file contents in hex and ASCII

SYNOPSIS
       hexdump [-C] [-n length] [-s skip] [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
       Prints each file as canonical hex plus ASCII: an offset, sixteen
       bytes of hex, then the printable form.

OPTIONS
       -C       canonical output (the default)
       -n N     stop after N bytes
       -s OFF   start OFF bytes into the file
       -v       do not compress repeated lines (accepted, no-op)

EXAMPLES
       hexdump -n 64 /usr/share/media/giphy.gif

SEE ALSO
       hexed(1), cat(1), dd(1)
